WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:05.265 --> 00:00:07.506
<i>[narrator]: In Toronto's
war on crime.</i>

2
00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.885
<i>the worst offenders
are pursued by the detectives</i>

3
00:00:09.886 --> 00:00:12.851
<i>of the Specialized Criminal
Investigations Unit.</i>

4
00:00:12.852 --> 00:00:14.333
<i>These are their stories.</i>

5
00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:15.540
[echoing gavel]

6
00:00:15.541 --> 00:00:17.989
[laughter and chatter]

7
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.161
- Loves to cook.

8
00:00:20.162 --> 00:00:22.162
All right.
two or more languages.

9
00:00:23.472 --> 00:00:25.334
[chuckling]
You lot are putting me to shame.

10
00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:27.954
All right. what about
loves live performance?

11
00:00:27.955 --> 00:00:29.196
- Hm.

12
00:00:29.852 --> 00:00:32.678
- Huh. Jim Coer. Peter Buff.

13
00:00:32.679 --> 00:00:34.609
Edwin. we could be twins.

14
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.885
[chuckling]
- Back home. I once did

15
00:00:36.886 --> 00:00:39.920
costume design for
a theatre company in Nairobi.

16
00:00:39.921 --> 00:00:42.920
I. uh. made this tie. actually.

17
00:00:42.921 --> 00:00:45.540
[scoffs]
- All right. Forget twins.

18
00:00:45.541 --> 00:00:47.506
You have way too much time.
[chuckling]

19
00:00:47.507 --> 00:00:49.023
I bet you're proud of your son.

20
00:00:49.024 --> 00:00:50.368
- Would you care to try

21
00:00:50.369 --> 00:00:51.921
Len's famous
date and walnut cookies?

22
00:00:54.265 --> 00:00:55.610
Have fun.

23
00:00:56.852 --> 00:01:00.023
- All right. so.
drinks coffee or tea...

24
00:01:00.024 --> 00:01:01.713
[water running]
- Hey. Adam.

25
00:01:01.714 --> 00:01:03.023
Oof. what happened there?

26
00:01:03.024 --> 00:01:05.713
- Sprained tendon.
Just hit the bag wrong.

27
00:01:05.714 --> 00:01:07.920
- I used to do a bit
of boxing back in the day.

28
00:01:07.921 --> 00:01:10.196
Wrist support is everything.
- Yeah. thanks.

29
00:01:11.679 --> 00:01:13.748
- Hey. Tevin.
- Welcome back. Len.

30
00:01:15.438 --> 00:01:17.921
[intriguing music]

31
00:01:24.748 --> 00:01:26.057
- Wait. a room?

32
00:01:26.058 --> 00:01:29.126
[chuckling]
Babe. it's a den.

33
00:01:29.127 --> 00:01:30.678
It doesn't even have a door.

34
00:01:30.679 --> 00:01:32.644
- Yeah. but I have
a nutribullet.

35
00:01:32.645 --> 00:01:34.402
- I thought that broke.

36
00:01:34.403 --> 00:01:36.438
- Which is why
I need the roommate.

37
00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:39.575
Whoa. Hi.

38
00:01:39.576 --> 00:01:41.264
- You don't tape over
someone's face.

39
00:01:41.265 --> 00:01:43.161
- It's old news. Hazel.

40
00:01:43.162 --> 00:01:45.023
- That doesn't mean
it's yours to cover.

41
00:01:45.024 --> 00:01:47.024
- All right. my bad.

42
00:01:49.955 --> 00:01:52.955
[suspenseful music]

43
00:01:54.955 --> 00:01:57.126
♪ Move to the left
if you have a few left ♪

44
00:01:57.127 --> 00:01:59.057
♪ Slide to the right
'cause I know it ain't right ♪

45
00:01:59.058 --> 00:02:01.299
♪ Drop down low 'cause you
already know that you fly ♪

46
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.092
♪ Jump up
if you're feeling the high ♪

47
00:02:03.093 --> 00:02:05.092
♪ Step to the back
'cause you're never going back ♪

48
00:02:05.093 --> 00:02:06.954
♪ Pump to the front 'cause
you're never gonna front ♪

49
00:02:06.955 --> 00:02:08.678
♪ Boy. now I know
that it's true ♪

50
00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:11.299
♪ It's not me. boy.
it's not me. it's you ♪

51
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.506
[rhythmic music]

52
00:02:13.507 --> 00:02:16.437
- Thanks for bringing me.
- Oh. don't mention it.

53
00:02:16.438 --> 00:02:18.126
I've been where you are.

54
00:02:18.127 --> 00:02:20.609
- It's two doubles.
[glasses thudding]

55
00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.023
And. uh... I'm single.

56
00:02:23.024 --> 00:02:24.678
- Uh. leave the kid alone.

57
00:02:24.679 --> 00:02:26.300
[chuckling]
We're gonna find a spot.

58
00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.783
- Hey! Are you holding?

59
00:02:37.472 --> 00:02:39.817
- I know. I know.
You drop it. I stack it.

60
00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.610
- Davie.
what can I get you to drink?

61
00:02:45.645 --> 00:02:48.264
[police sirens afar]
- What exactly are they saying?

62
00:02:48.265 --> 00:02:50.989
Well. let them spin the story
however they want.

63
00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:52.713
As long as my name
doesn't come up.

64
00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:54.989
[muffled booming club music]

65
00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:58.231
Yeah. all right. thanks.
Keep me posted.

66
00:02:59.024 --> 00:03:00.609
<i>[dispatch over radio]:
Are you there. Webb?</i>

67
00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.816
<i>There's a traffic incident
at Church and Wellesley.</i>

68
00:03:02.817 --> 00:03:04.644
[engine starts]

69
00:03:04.645 --> 00:03:06.472
- Webb here.
currently unavailable.

70
00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:10.644
[indistinct shouting]

71
00:03:10.645 --> 00:03:12.575
[club music stops abruptly]

72
00:03:12.576 --> 00:03:14.678
- Hey. take it easy on him.

73
00:03:14.679 --> 00:03:16.230
He just wants to see the show.

74
00:03:16.231 --> 00:03:19.161
- You don't speak to me
about my son.

75
00:03:19.162 --> 00:03:23.092
Let that be your first
and last mistake.

76
00:03:23.093 --> 00:03:25.955
[suspenseful music builds]

77
00:03:27.541 --> 00:03:29.506
- So I said
if she wants a nanny.

78
00:03:29.507 --> 00:03:31.368
she can pay the payroll tax.

79
00:03:31.369 --> 00:03:33.264
[gasping]
- God. Em.

80
00:03:33.265 --> 00:03:35.299
you're. like. the only woman
I know that can't cardio

81
00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.403
and gossip at the same time.

82
00:03:39.231 --> 00:03:40.472
[shaky breathing]

83
00:03:45.127 --> 00:03:47.196
[theme music]

84
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

85
00:04:23.058 --> 00:04:24.920
- Couple of locals were getting
their morning steps in

86
00:04:24.921 --> 00:04:26.368
when they spotted him.

87
00:04:26.369 --> 00:04:29.023
Call came in at 6:30 AM.

88
00:04:29.024 --> 00:04:30.920
[police radios chirping]
- Any other witnesses?

89
00:04:30.921 --> 00:04:32.678
- Canvassing. but nothing yet.

90
00:04:32.679 --> 00:04:35.782
We got a line search underway
to look for the murder weapon.

91
00:04:35.783 --> 00:04:38.092
The assault started
up there on the pathway.

92
00:04:38.093 --> 00:04:40.093
continued down. ended here.

93
00:04:41.231 --> 00:04:43.057
- Blunt force to the head.

94
00:04:43.058 --> 00:04:45.264
Heavy on the trauma.
[exhaling]

95
00:04:45.265 --> 00:04:48.024
- You got a name?
- Len Marsden. 55.

96
00:04:49.541 --> 00:04:52.333
- Cash. credit cards.
looks like it's all here.

97
00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.161
- Been working this
neighbourhood for a long time.

98
00:04:54.162 --> 00:04:57.333
Muggings are rare.
Murders... rarer.

99
00:04:57.334 --> 00:05:01.402
- Well. Rosedale's not exactly
a... hotbed of sin.

100
00:05:01.403 --> 00:05:04.471
Quiet. rich.
One of the lowest crime rates

101
00:05:04.472 --> 00:05:07.402
in the country. actually.
Nice gig.

102
00:05:07.403 --> 00:05:09.264
- It was up until this morning.

103
00:05:09.265 --> 00:05:11.471
- Maybe it was a crime
of opportunity.

104
00:05:11.472 --> 00:05:13.816
Killer waited for
the perfect moment.

105
00:05:13.817 --> 00:05:15.540
Strikes hard. then moved on.

106
00:05:15.541 --> 00:05:18.471
- Moved over this way.

107
00:05:18.472 --> 00:05:20.747
A freshly dug hole.

108
00:05:20.748 --> 00:05:22.541
[intriguing music]

109
00:05:25.472 --> 00:05:27.471
- Oh. boy.
- Looks like the killer

110
00:05:27.472 --> 00:05:29.782
was planning on
burying the body.

111
00:05:29.783 --> 00:05:31.645
Maybe something
interrupted them.

112
00:05:32.955 --> 00:05:35.438
- The park lights are on timers.

113
00:05:36.265 --> 00:05:39.299
Set to come on at dusk
and turn off at dawn.

114
00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:42.471
That one's still on.
Its timer must be faulty.

115
00:05:42.472 --> 00:05:44.299
And maybe the attack
happened at night.

116
00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:48.300
Light kicked on and spooked
the killer mid burial.

117
00:05:49.679 --> 00:05:53.437
- Time of death is between
11 PM and two AM last night.

118
00:05:53.438 --> 00:05:56.264
Cause of death. multiple
traumatic blows to the head.

119
00:05:56.265 --> 00:05:58.092
And when I say multiple.
I mean that our victim

120
00:05:58.093 --> 00:06:00.092
took a serious beating.
He was dead

121
00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.368
before the final blow
even landed.

122
00:06:01.369 --> 00:06:02.989
- So. serious overkill.

123
00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:04.368
Uh. what'd they use?

124
00:06:04.369 --> 00:06:06.540
- Some blunt baton-like weapon.

125
00:06:06.541 --> 00:06:08.195
- Any signs he fought back?

126
00:06:08.196 --> 00:06:09.851
- None. No defensive wounds.

127
00:06:09.852 --> 00:06:11.678
- It's hard to believe
a man of Len's size

128
00:06:11.679 --> 00:06:13.195
would go down without a fight.

129
00:06:13.196 --> 00:06:15.540
- He didn't defend himself
because he couldn't.

130
00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.885
Toxicology turned up
a high blood alcohol level

131
00:06:17.886 --> 00:06:19.575
and a high dose of ketamine.

132
00:06:19.576 --> 00:06:21.851
Both ingested less than
an hour before he died.

133
00:06:21.852 --> 00:06:24.057
- So. essentially.
he was legless

134
00:06:24.058 --> 00:06:25.920
by the time he got
on the path.

135
00:06:25.921 --> 00:06:27.609
- Do we know
what Len was doing

136
00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:29.368
on the path so late
in the first place?

137
00:06:29.369 --> 00:06:30.851
- His apartment's in Rosedale.

138
00:06:30.852 --> 00:06:32.264
Ten-minute walk
from the crime scene.

139
00:06:32.265 --> 00:06:34.161
- So. maybe somebody saw him

140
00:06:34.162 --> 00:06:35.954
drunk. drugged. walking alone.

141
00:06:35.955 --> 00:06:37.678
decided to take advantage.

142
00:06:37.679 --> 00:06:39.333
- Could be.
Or it's just as possible

143
00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:41.023
that somebody wanted him
in that state.

144
00:06:41.024 --> 00:06:43.161
As Bateman says.
look at the size of the guy.

145
00:06:43.162 --> 00:06:44.851
He'd be a lot easier
to handle like that.

146
00:06:44.852 --> 00:06:48.299
- No next of kin.
no financial activity yesterday.

147
00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.540
Well. The man had nobody.

148
00:06:50.541 --> 00:06:52.989
and yet half of Rosedale
is calling in.

149
00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:54.782
demanding to know
what happened to him.

150
00:06:54.783 --> 00:06:56.575
- Okay. we'll head to his place.

151
00:06:56.576 --> 00:06:58.920
[sighing]
Build a timeline forward.

152
00:06:58.921 --> 00:07:02.506
Find out why big Len here
didn't make it home last night.

153
00:07:02.507 --> 00:07:05.299
- Remember what they did
to Jamie's son. Levi?

154
00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.955
When they caught him
with the neighbour boy.

155
00:07:11.093 --> 00:07:14.885
They dragged him through
their village. Flogged him.

156
00:07:14.886 --> 00:07:16.609
Until he stopped breathing.

157
00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:18.747
- It's not like that here.
- Edwin.

158
00:07:18.748 --> 00:07:20.954
do you think I wanted
to do that last night?

159
00:07:20.955 --> 00:07:23.299
I had to for you.

160
00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:28.471
- Len. Len didn't deserve--
- Never speak that name again.

161
00:07:28.472 --> 00:07:30.300
[echoing gavel]

162
00:07:32.921 --> 00:07:34.575
[papers crumpling]

163
00:07:34.576 --> 00:07:36.092
[sighing]
- Give me something.

164
00:07:36.093 --> 00:07:37.713
Where are you?

165
00:07:37.714 --> 00:07:39.472
[intriguing music]

166
00:07:42.265 --> 00:07:43.920
[sighing]

167
00:07:43.921 --> 00:07:45.609
- Spoke with Len's landlord.

168
00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.575
Last time she saw him
was yesterday.

169
00:07:47.576 --> 00:07:50.230
He was pulling out
in his van around noon.

170
00:07:50.231 --> 00:07:51.747
- His van's back
in the parking spot?

171
00:07:51.748 --> 00:07:54.230
- No. actually.
just flagged it with CPIC.

172
00:07:54.231 --> 00:07:56.713
Patrol are watching out for...
What? What'd you find?

173
00:07:56.714 --> 00:07:59.678
- A calendar entry.
Yesterday at noon.

174
00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:01.816
N.H.U.

175
00:08:01.817 --> 00:08:04.126
- N.H.U.
Could be someone's initials?

176
00:08:04.127 --> 00:08:06.299
- No.

177
00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.299
New Haven United Church.

178
00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.472
- Amen.

179
00:08:10.852 --> 00:08:13.540
- Len was a self-employed
handyman.

180
00:08:13.541 --> 00:08:15.816
I've been contracting him
for years.

181
00:08:15.817 --> 00:08:17.954
He's dependable. quiet.

182
00:08:17.955 --> 00:08:20.437
Always got the job done.
- You two were close.

183
00:08:20.438 --> 00:08:22.195
- Not at first.

184
00:08:22.196 --> 00:08:23.782
He mostly kept to himself.

185
00:08:23.783 --> 00:08:25.368
But. uh. a few years back.

186
00:08:25.369 --> 00:08:27.471
I asked him if he would help
with some renovations.

187
00:08:27.472 --> 00:08:29.885
Pews. benches.
that sort of thing.

188
00:08:29.886 --> 00:08:31.402
And then he was around a lot.

189
00:08:31.403 --> 00:08:34.023
- And did that change things
between the two of you?

190
00:08:34.024 --> 00:08:36.678
- New Haven is a very
inclusive space

191
00:08:36.679 --> 00:08:38.678
and Len could see that.

192
00:08:38.679 --> 00:08:42.369
Soon enough. he was a beloved
member of the congregation.

193
00:08:44.024 --> 00:08:45.954
This is gonna upset
a lot of people.

194
00:08:45.955 --> 00:08:47.644
- Anyone in particular?

195
00:08:47.645 --> 00:08:51.747
Someone that he'd been seeing
a lot more of lately?

196
00:08:51.748 --> 00:08:53.851
- A young man named Edwin.

197
00:08:53.852 --> 00:08:55.782
Uh. Kenyan. newcomer.

198
00:08:55.783 --> 00:08:59.609
They met at a new Canadian tea
recently and got on well.

199
00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:04.092
Edwin stopped by
yesterday to see Len.

200
00:09:04.093 --> 00:09:06.368
They left together around seven.

201
00:09:06.369 --> 00:09:08.299
- Did he mention
where they were going?

202
00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:10.023
- No.

203
00:09:10.024 --> 00:09:12.678
But. strangely.
I got an email this morning

204
00:09:12.679 --> 00:09:14.678
from Edwin's father. Jeremiah.

205
00:09:14.679 --> 00:09:17.989
He asked to be taken off
the church event's mailing list.

206
00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.023
I got the sense that...

207
00:09:20.024 --> 00:09:22.023
he wasn't comfortable with
Len and Edwin's friendship.

208
00:09:22.024 --> 00:09:23.576
- Thank you.

209
00:09:26.024 --> 00:09:27.782
[echoing gavel]

210
00:09:27.783 --> 00:09:29.747
I just came
from New Haven Church.

211
00:09:29.748 --> 00:09:32.747
Minister Cade
informed me that. um.

212
00:09:32.748 --> 00:09:34.713
he received a strange
request from you.

213
00:09:34.714 --> 00:09:37.230
Why did you send that email?

214
00:09:37.231 --> 00:09:40.368
- I could not continue
to accept help from a church

215
00:09:40.369 --> 00:09:42.195
that welcomes people like Len.

216
00:09:42.196 --> 00:09:44.023
- Len was just like me.

217
00:09:44.024 --> 00:09:46.092
[heavy breathing]
He understood what it was like

218
00:09:46.093 --> 00:09:47.747
to have a father
who couldn't accept him

219
00:09:47.748 --> 00:09:49.747
for who he was.

220
00:09:49.748 --> 00:09:52.368
- After you and Len left
the church yesterday.

221
00:09:52.369 --> 00:09:54.471
where did you go?
- He knew I was looking

222
00:09:54.472 --> 00:09:56.057
for a queer community
in Toronto.

223
00:09:56.058 --> 00:10:00.057
so he offered to take me
to a drag show.

224
00:10:00.058 --> 00:10:01.540
- I went to this show
to get him.

225
00:10:01.541 --> 00:10:04.161
He was drunk. dancing.

226
00:10:04.162 --> 00:10:06.402
- So what'd you do?
- I raised my voice.

227
00:10:06.403 --> 00:10:08.782
- Is that all?
- Broke some glasses.

228
00:10:08.783 --> 00:10:12.713
I won't deny it.
but no one was hurt.

229
00:10:12.714 --> 00:10:14.713
- My father brought me
straight home

230
00:10:14.714 --> 00:10:17.092
and we've been here ever since.

231
00:10:17.093 --> 00:10:19.092
When. uh.
we left that drag show.

232
00:10:19.093 --> 00:10:22.264
Len was a little drunk.
but very much alive.

233
00:10:22.265 --> 00:10:24.264
- Did you see any drugs?
Ketamine?

234
00:10:24.265 --> 00:10:27.748
- I don't know what that is.
I just wanted to see the show.

235
00:10:28.231 --> 00:10:31.195
- Okay.
Uh. and where was this show?

236
00:10:31.196 --> 00:10:32.644
- Crews & Tangos.

237
00:10:32.645 --> 00:10:36.747
It's a bar in an area Len called
the Gay Village.

238
00:10:36.748 --> 00:10:38.921
[tense music]

239
00:10:40.127 --> 00:10:42.368
Back home.

240
00:10:42.369 --> 00:10:45.471
being gay can get you killed
by your family.

241
00:10:45.472 --> 00:10:47.264
My father is scared

242
00:10:47.265 --> 00:10:49.368
what happened to Len
could happen to me.

243
00:10:49.369 --> 00:10:52.507
But he's not a bad man.

244
00:10:53.507 --> 00:10:56.333
- Father said the. uh.
confrontation wasn't violent

245
00:10:56.334 --> 00:10:58.713
and they left Crews & Tangos
around nine.

246
00:10:58.714 --> 00:11:00.092
- Kid's telling the same story.

247
00:11:00.093 --> 00:11:02.161
He claims they haven't left
the apartment since.

248
00:11:02.162 --> 00:11:04.816
- Da Silva says that Len
had his last drink

249
00:11:04.817 --> 00:11:07.057
and took the drugs
in the hour before he died.

250
00:11:07.058 --> 00:11:09.471
so no earlier than 10 PM.

251
00:11:09.472 --> 00:11:10.954
If their alibi holds--

252
00:11:10.955 --> 00:11:12.437
- Edwin would've been
long gone

253
00:11:12.438 --> 00:11:14.333
before he'd even have
the chance to dose Len.

254
00:11:14.334 --> 00:11:16.507
- So let's find out
who stuck around.

255
00:11:17.541 --> 00:11:18.921
[echoing gavel]

256
00:11:20.472 --> 00:11:22.299
[booming club music]
- Who was Len talking to

257
00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:23.851
after Edwin and his father left?

258
00:11:23.852 --> 00:11:25.506
- I couldn't tell you.
It was drag night.

259
00:11:25.507 --> 00:11:28.264
the place is packed.
I served Len and Edwin

260
00:11:28.265 --> 00:11:31.299
around eight. saw them again
during all the drama.

261
00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.713
And didn't pay much attention
to Len after that.

262
00:11:33.714 --> 00:11:36.195
- You know. our pathologist
told us that. uh.

263
00:11:36.196 --> 00:11:39.126
by the time this guy left.
he could barely walk.

264
00:11:39.127 --> 00:11:40.851
So. who was the last
to serve him?

265
00:11:40.852 --> 00:11:42.506
- Any one of the other
bartenders?

266
00:11:42.507 --> 00:11:44.851
Or my manager. Hazel.

267
00:11:44.852 --> 00:11:47.713
She might have stepped in.
She knew Len better than I did.

268
00:11:47.714 --> 00:11:49.920
- And where is she now?
- Upstairs bar.

269
00:11:49.921 --> 00:11:51.540
- One last question.

270
00:11:51.541 --> 00:11:53.920
Do you know where Len
might've found ketamine in here?

271
00:11:53.921 --> 00:11:55.437
- Yeah. no.

272
00:11:55.438 --> 00:11:57.747
But. place like this.
night like that.

273
00:11:57.748 --> 00:11:59.024
wouldn't take much asking.

274
00:11:59.817 --> 00:12:01.678
- Thanks.
- Mm-hmm.

275
00:12:01.679 --> 00:12:03.852
[booming bar music continues]

276
00:12:07.507 --> 00:12:09.126
- Cut him off around 10:30.

277
00:12:09.127 --> 00:12:11.540
Len didn't come in
that often. but...

278
00:12:11.541 --> 00:12:13.471
I think after that argument
with that kid's dad.

279
00:12:13.472 --> 00:12:15.333
he overdid it a bit.

280
00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:17.230
Drugs. though. I don't know
where those came from.

281
00:12:17.231 --> 00:12:19.161
- Did you happen to notice
Len hanging out

282
00:12:19.162 --> 00:12:21.885
or leaving with anyone?
- No.

283
00:12:21.886 --> 00:12:23.885
But I was up here bartending
for most of the night.

284
00:12:23.886 --> 00:12:25.989
He was downstairs.
- I noticed a couple of these

285
00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:27.402
posters up the block.

286
00:12:27.403 --> 00:12:29.506
but. uh.
it was a different name.

287
00:12:29.507 --> 00:12:32.851
Omar and. uh. Yusuf.

288
00:12:32.852 --> 00:12:35.264
These yours?
- Yeah. Len and I were gonna go

289
00:12:35.265 --> 00:12:37.920
canvassing in Cabbagetown
this afternoon.

290
00:12:37.921 --> 00:12:40.678
- Hm. the two of you
were searching for these men?

291
00:12:40.679 --> 00:12:43.575
- Yes.
Us along with some others.

292
00:12:43.576 --> 00:12:46.230
That's how we met.
- Did Len know any of these men?

293
00:12:46.231 --> 00:12:47.885
- No.

294
00:12:47.886 --> 00:12:49.506
But the village
is pretty tight-knit.

295
00:12:49.507 --> 00:12:51.954
You know. it's big and small
at the same time.

296
00:12:51.955 --> 00:12:53.437
[Bateman]: And what have
the police turned up?

297
00:12:53.438 --> 00:12:55.989
- Nothing.
They're brown-skinned.

298
00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:59.231
Gay. They're living
on the edge of society.

299
00:12:59.955 --> 00:13:01.954
[shutter clicking]
It's nothing new. though.

300
00:13:01.955 --> 00:13:03.437
The cops in this community
are enforcers.

301
00:13:03.438 --> 00:13:05.058
not protectors.

302
00:13:07.231 --> 00:13:09.609
What happened to Len is awful.

303
00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:12.816
but if it had happened in
the village instead of Rosedale.

304
00:13:12.817 --> 00:13:14.885
who knows how seriously
the local police

305
00:13:14.886 --> 00:13:16.368
would've taken
the investigation?

306
00:13:16.369 --> 00:13:18.851
- So. all these men went missing
from the village

307
00:13:18.852 --> 00:13:20.368
within the last two years?

308
00:13:20.369 --> 00:13:22.954
- Yes.
Pattern's obvious to us.

309
00:13:22.955 --> 00:13:25.438
Even though the cops pretend
like it doesn't mean anything.

310
00:13:26.369 --> 00:13:30.126
- You think the same person's
behind these disappearances.

311
00:13:30.127 --> 00:13:31.713
- You see it. don't you?

312
00:13:31.714 --> 00:13:33.955
[intriguing music swelling]

313
00:13:39.334 --> 00:13:41.575
- Alright. let's say that
the village is on to something.

314
00:13:41.576 --> 00:13:44.230
How does Len Marsden
fit in with this picture?

315
00:13:44.231 --> 00:13:46.437
- Well. he obviously doesn't
match the racial profile.

316
00:13:46.438 --> 00:13:48.851
but he does fit a pattern.

317
00:13:48.852 --> 00:13:51.782
Middle-aged. bearded.
bigger bodied.

318
00:13:51.783 --> 00:13:54.265
All these men self-identified
as bears.

319
00:13:54.748 --> 00:13:56.713
The demography tracks.

320
00:13:56.714 --> 00:13:58.161
- As does the geography.

321
00:13:58.162 --> 00:14:00.575
Omar. Yusuf. and Arjun
were all last seen

322
00:14:00.576 --> 00:14:02.540
within a kilometre
of each other.

323
00:14:02.541 --> 00:14:06.023
And Len was likely drugged
at Crews & Tangos.

324
00:14:06.024 --> 00:14:08.368
which is smack dab in the middle
of that area.

325
00:14:08.369 --> 00:14:10.402
- And if these other
three men are dead.

326
00:14:10.403 --> 00:14:11.816
where are their bodies?

327
00:14:11.817 --> 00:14:14.195
Because Len's body
turned up on that trail.

328
00:14:14.196 --> 00:14:16.368
- We found a shallow grave
at the scene.

329
00:14:16.369 --> 00:14:18.920
We're thinking the killer
intended to bury Len.

330
00:14:18.921 --> 00:14:21.368
but. uh. didn't get the chance
to finish the job.

331
00:14:21.369 --> 00:14:24.747
- And serial killers get caught
when they get sloppy.

332
00:14:24.748 --> 00:14:26.609
This might be
their first slip up.

333
00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:29.264
- All right. put a team
on the Ravine Trail.

334
00:14:29.265 --> 00:14:31.437
Have them search
for other graves

335
00:14:31.438 --> 00:14:35.610
and follow up with whoever
handled the missing men's cases.

336
00:14:37.886 --> 00:14:39.610
[echoing gavel]

337
00:14:41.162 --> 00:14:42.920
- Officer Webb.
how long you've been

338
00:14:42.921 --> 00:14:45.437
running point on the. uh.
village detail?

339
00:14:45.438 --> 00:14:47.057
- Few years now.

340
00:14:47.058 --> 00:14:48.540
Big on outreach.

341
00:14:48.541 --> 00:14:50.644
Boots on the ground.

342
00:14:50.645 --> 00:14:52.057
My team's done
a really good job

343
00:14:52.058 --> 00:14:53.852
at keeping lines
of communication open.

344
00:14:54.714 --> 00:14:57.506
- So. you've heard about this.
uh. serial killer theory?

345
00:14:57.507 --> 00:15:00.023
- Only at every town hall
since last winter.

346
00:15:00.024 --> 00:15:02.678
Really picked up after
Akeem Shadid disappeared.

347
00:15:02.679 --> 00:15:05.437
- Akeem Shadid? I-I don't
remember Hazel mentioning him.

348
00:15:05.438 --> 00:15:07.678
- She wouldn't.

349
00:15:07.679 --> 00:15:10.437
Akeem was living
with schizophrenia.

350
00:15:10.438 --> 00:15:12.161
He vanished
for a couple of months.

351
00:15:12.162 --> 00:15:14.092
turned up in Timmins.
alive and unharmed.

352
00:15:14.093 --> 00:15:16.540
but by then.
Hazel had already lit the match.

353
00:15:16.541 --> 00:15:18.678
Accused us of ignoring
a killer in the village.

354
00:15:18.679 --> 00:15:20.713
Folks got scared.

355
00:15:20.714 --> 00:15:23.195
- So what's your take
on Hazel's. um.

356
00:15:23.196 --> 00:15:25.713
serial killer theory?

357
00:15:25.714 --> 00:15:28.437
- Omar Haddad. Yusuf Nassar.
Arjun Patel.

358
00:15:28.438 --> 00:15:30.540
I've looked in all of them.

359
00:15:30.541 --> 00:15:32.540
We didn't find any signs
of foul play.

360
00:15:32.541 --> 00:15:34.023
- Hm. and what did you find?

361
00:15:34.024 --> 00:15:36.816
- Omar had a long history
of drug use.

362
00:15:36.817 --> 00:15:38.885
Arjun was a sex worker
and unhoused.

363
00:15:38.886 --> 00:15:40.713
Yusuf's refugee claim
was denied.

364
00:15:40.714 --> 00:15:42.644
He-he might've gone underground.

365
00:15:42.645 --> 00:15:44.023
But these aren't
the kinds of guys

366
00:15:44.024 --> 00:15:45.368
who leave a forwarding
address.

367
00:15:45.369 --> 00:15:47.126
- No. but they are
the kind of guys

368
00:15:47.127 --> 00:15:49.575
whose disappearance wouldn't

369
00:15:49.576 --> 00:15:51.644
cause headlines.
and the kind of guys

370
00:15:51.645 --> 00:15:54.644
who somebody could pick off
without much noise.

371
00:15:54.645 --> 00:15:56.747
- Look. I walked this strip
longer than most.

372
00:15:56.748 --> 00:15:58.575
I think I got a good idea
of who's out there

373
00:15:58.576 --> 00:15:59.954
and who's just moved on.

374
00:15:59.955 --> 00:16:01.678
Look. not every gap
in a community

375
00:16:01.679 --> 00:16:03.057
is evidence of foul play.

376
00:16:03.058 --> 00:16:04.437
- Yeah. you're probably right.

377
00:16:04.438 --> 00:16:06.368
Still. there's just a few things

378
00:16:06.369 --> 00:16:08.713
we wanna cross reference
with our investigation

379
00:16:08.714 --> 00:16:11.264
in. uh. Len Marsden's murder.

380
00:16:11.265 --> 00:16:12.989
- Yeah. yeah.
How about I pull my notes

381
00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:14.816
and I have them sent over
to your office?

382
00:16:14.817 --> 00:16:16.678
- Appreciate it.

383
00:16:16.679 --> 00:16:18.610
[tense music]

384
00:16:19.679 --> 00:16:21.851
- Just got off the phone
with the last of the witnesses

385
00:16:21.852 --> 00:16:24.678
Webb interviewed
in the missing men's cases.

386
00:16:24.679 --> 00:16:26.885
- And?
- And their statements

387
00:16:26.886 --> 00:16:28.920
haven't changed.
Webb's notes line up.

388
00:16:28.921 --> 00:16:30.402
I asked them about Len

389
00:16:30.403 --> 00:16:32.264
and there doesn't seem
to be any connection.

390
00:16:32.265 --> 00:16:34.092
[indistinct office chatter]

391
00:16:34.093 --> 00:16:36.713
- We're missing something.
[inhaling sharply]

392
00:16:36.714 --> 00:16:39.023
What were these men doing
when they disappeared?

393
00:16:39.024 --> 00:16:40.609
- We don't really know.

394
00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:44.540
Uh. Yusuf and Arjun
were last seen at intersections

395
00:16:44.541 --> 00:16:47.851
and Omar was last seen leaving
his building on Dundonald.

396
00:16:47.852 --> 00:16:50.092
- Did Omar live with anyone?

397
00:16:50.093 --> 00:16:52.093
- Yeah. Ziggy Stardust.

398
00:16:53.265 --> 00:16:55.920
His dog. Apparently. it barked
for three days straight

399
00:16:55.921 --> 00:16:57.575
after Omar went missing.
the poor thing.

400
00:16:57.576 --> 00:16:58.747
Neighbour called it in.

401
00:16:58.748 --> 00:17:00.161
[office phone ringing]

402
00:17:00.162 --> 00:17:03.368
- No. Arjun and Yusuf
were of no fixed address.

403
00:17:03.369 --> 00:17:05.506
Len and Omar lived alone.

404
00:17:05.507 --> 00:17:07.885
Now. that's not something
you learn about

405
00:17:07.886 --> 00:17:09.264
somebody at a glance.

406
00:17:09.265 --> 00:17:10.989
- The killer knew them.

407
00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:13.126
Knew there wouldn't be anyone
waiting for them at home

408
00:17:13.127 --> 00:17:15.264
or that there wasn't even
any home to begin with.

409
00:17:15.265 --> 00:17:17.057
- Yeah.
The missing connection

410
00:17:17.058 --> 00:17:19.678
is where the killer
was meeting his victims.

411
00:17:19.679 --> 00:17:23.437
Learning who would
quietly disappear.

412
00:17:23.438 --> 00:17:25.644
We find that place.

413
00:17:25.645 --> 00:17:27.783
we find the killer's
hunting ground.

414
00:17:28.334 --> 00:17:30.678
- None of the other victims
came to my bar.

415
00:17:30.679 --> 00:17:32.299
There was a little cafe
over on Maitland.

416
00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.575
Omar used to grab coffee
there sometimes.

417
00:17:34.576 --> 00:17:36.782
And Arjun would get pastries
from their food rescue program

418
00:17:36.783 --> 00:17:38.195
when he needed to.

419
00:17:38.196 --> 00:17:39.851
- Yeah. we spoke
with the owner there.

420
00:17:39.852 --> 00:17:42.092
Her statement was
in their case files.

421
00:17:42.093 --> 00:17:43.747
so she said
they would come in alone.

422
00:17:43.748 --> 00:17:45.747
no conversations. no company.

423
00:17:45.748 --> 00:17:46.989
- What about Yusuf?

424
00:17:46.990 --> 00:17:49.264
Um. any interactions
with the others?

425
00:17:49.265 --> 00:17:51.402
- Yusuf kept to himself
more than most.

426
00:17:51.403 --> 00:17:53.507
Moved around like he was trying
not to be seen.

427
00:17:54.369 --> 00:17:57.333
Heard he was closeted.
- And facing deportation.

428
00:17:57.334 --> 00:17:59.541
To someone like that.
discretion is key.

429
00:18:00.714 --> 00:18:03.057
- So. where might
Yusuf have gone

430
00:18:03.058 --> 00:18:04.885
if he wanted
to meet men discreetly?

431
00:18:04.886 --> 00:18:07.023
- A bathhouse.

432
00:18:07.024 --> 00:18:10.230
Doesn't get more discreet
than that.

433
00:18:10.231 --> 00:18:11.230
Like. now.

434
00:18:11.231 --> 00:18:13.196
[soft music playing in bar]

435
00:18:15.714 --> 00:18:19.989
- Low lights. private rooms.
no cameras. unspoken

436
00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:23.368
understanding that. uh. people
don't talk about what they see.

437
00:18:23.369 --> 00:18:25.816
A bathhouse is a perfect place
for a predator

438
00:18:25.817 --> 00:18:30.161
to get close to their target
without too many eyes on them.

439
00:18:30.162 --> 00:18:33.126
- Yeah. sure is.
Only three bathhouses

440
00:18:33.127 --> 00:18:35.127
within walking distance.
Take your pick.

441
00:18:36.024 --> 00:18:38.333
- Steamhaus Baths logo.

442
00:18:38.334 --> 00:18:39.713
- Yeah.
- That's the same logo

443
00:18:39.714 --> 00:18:41.955
that was on Len's gym bag
in his apartment.

444
00:18:44.541 --> 00:18:46.024
[echoing gavel]

445
00:18:47.231 --> 00:18:48.885
[typing on keyboard]

446
00:18:48.886 --> 00:18:50.402
[indistinct chatter]

447
00:18:50.403 --> 00:18:53.162
- And no Len Marsden.

448
00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:55.989
[chuckling]
Look. detectives.

449
00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:58.644
if these men were members
of my bathhouse. I would know.

450
00:18:58.645 --> 00:19:01.092
- Well. that's strange.
because Len's bank records

451
00:19:01.093 --> 00:19:03.264
show he's been a member
here for years.

452
00:19:03.265 --> 00:19:04.817
[suspenseful music]

453
00:19:05.645 --> 00:19:07.264
Where were you
the night Len died?

454
00:19:07.265 --> 00:19:10.885
- Here. We're open 24/7.

455
00:19:10.886 --> 00:19:12.954
There were over a hundred guys
through here that night.

456
00:19:12.955 --> 00:19:14.471
Ask any of them.

457
00:19:14.472 --> 00:19:17.369
- Tevin. did you delete
Len's membership?

458
00:19:19.024 --> 00:19:21.575
He's not saying no.
- Mm.

459
00:19:21.576 --> 00:19:25.126
So. if you didn't have anything
to do with Len's murder.

460
00:19:25.127 --> 00:19:26.645
why'd you scrub his name?

461
00:19:28.058 --> 00:19:30.230
- Because I was told to.

462
00:19:30.231 --> 00:19:32.024
- Told to? By whom?

463
00:19:33.472 --> 00:19:34.954
- It was Officer Webb.

464
00:19:34.955 --> 00:19:36.817
- What...
- Sorry?

465
00:19:38.058 --> 00:19:41.265
- What does Officer Webb
have to do with this?

466
00:19:42.955 --> 00:19:45.575
- When the posters
of the missing men

467
00:19:45.576 --> 00:19:47.609
started going up last winter.

468
00:19:47.610 --> 00:19:50.437
I realized that
they had all been here.

469
00:19:50.438 --> 00:19:52.093
shortly before
they disappeared.

470
00:19:53.231 --> 00:19:55.782
I caught Webb on patrol
and I told him about it.

471
00:19:55.783 --> 00:19:58.230
[chuckling]
But he said

472
00:19:58.231 --> 00:20:01.678
that the serial killer stuff
was all community panic.

473
00:20:01.679 --> 00:20:03.954
[sighing]
- And when did Webb tell you

474
00:20:03.955 --> 00:20:05.299
to wipe Len's name?

475
00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.333
- He cornered me
at my car last night.

476
00:20:07.334 --> 00:20:11.230
Told me that you might be
around asking about Len

477
00:20:11.231 --> 00:20:15.472
and the others and...
that I was to stay quiet.

478
00:20:18.403 --> 00:20:21.610
He said it wouldn't be
good for business.

479
00:20:22.955 --> 00:20:26.024
I know what it sounds like
when a cop makes a threat.

480
00:20:34.265 --> 00:20:37.196
- Damnit. I'm out.
- I'll grab more. Here.

481
00:20:40.921 --> 00:20:42.610
- Hey. need a hand?

482
00:20:43.783 --> 00:20:45.403
[tense music]

483
00:20:49.817 --> 00:20:52.195
Well. I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to scare you.

484
00:20:52.196 --> 00:20:53.471
- You didn't.

485
00:20:53.472 --> 00:20:56.334
- So. I heard you talking
to those detectives.

486
00:20:57.162 --> 00:20:59.471
So. you're back on
about that. um.

487
00:20:59.472 --> 00:21:01.713
serial killer theory again.

488
00:21:01.714 --> 00:21:04.333
- I didn't tell them anything
I haven't told you.

489
00:21:04.334 --> 00:21:06.678
More than once.
- Just remember.

490
00:21:06.679 --> 00:21:08.471
once the suits move on.

491
00:21:08.472 --> 00:21:10.954
me and my team
will still be here.

492
00:21:10.955 --> 00:21:12.368
looking out for folks.

493
00:21:12.369 --> 00:21:14.782
- Right. Looking out.

494
00:21:14.783 --> 00:21:17.195
- Is everything okay here?

495
00:21:17.196 --> 00:21:19.333
- Yeah. just making sure
everyone's safe.

496
00:21:19.334 --> 00:21:22.127
[tense music continues]

497
00:21:25.507 --> 00:21:27.540
[elevator dinging]

498
00:21:27.541 --> 00:21:29.609
- Obstructing an investigation

499
00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:32.609
and intimidating a witness
are serious claims.

500
00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:35.644
I'm gonna need more than
