758
00:33:15.507 --> 00:33:16.989
Hey. what is it?

759
00:33:16.990 --> 00:33:18.989
- Lucy said
there were six bodies.

760
00:33:18.990 --> 00:33:21.127
but we've only got
five trophies.

761
00:33:22.541 --> 00:33:25.092
One of them is missing.

762
00:33:25.093 --> 00:33:27.471
- So. turns out
there were more victims.

763
00:33:27.472 --> 00:33:29.645
I'm hearing
there were at least six.

764
00:33:30.645 --> 00:33:32.885
- That bastard. Len.
got what was coming to him.

765
00:33:32.886 --> 00:33:34.817
[approaching footsteps]

766
00:33:37.438 --> 00:33:39.264
- Benj.

767
00:33:39.265 --> 00:33:40.610
- See you tonight. Davie.
- Bye.

768
00:33:42.438 --> 00:33:44.989
- Thought I told you not
to bring that stuff in here.

769
00:33:44.990 --> 00:33:47.575
You can't take that outside?
- Where am I supposed to go?

770
00:33:47.576 --> 00:33:50.541
Reporters are on every block
asking about Len.

771
00:33:51.472 --> 00:33:54.885
- Is that my lighter? Benj.

772
00:33:54.886 --> 00:33:56.472
Come on. Hand it over.

773
00:33:57.300 --> 00:33:58.507
- Thank you.

774
00:33:59.403 --> 00:34:02.507
Don't worry.
I'm taking it outside.

775
00:34:06.576 --> 00:34:09.023
- Every major news outlet
is-is running the village

776
00:34:09.024 --> 00:34:11.230
serial killer story.
They're coming for Webb.

777
00:34:11.231 --> 00:34:13.161
asking how the hell
he missed the pattern.

778
00:34:13.162 --> 00:34:15.230
and where the oversight
was on his unit.

779
00:34:15.231 --> 00:34:17.678
- Won't be long before they're
asking about Len's killer. too.

780
00:34:17.679 --> 00:34:19.437
so where are we at with that?

781
00:34:19.438 --> 00:34:22.713
- Well. Len was targeting
and murdering vulnerable people

782
00:34:22.714 --> 00:34:24.195
from a marginalized community.

783
00:34:24.196 --> 00:34:25.851
He was showing
no signs of stopping

784
00:34:25.852 --> 00:34:27.402
and no one was doing
anything about it.

785
00:34:27.403 --> 00:34:28.816
The killer put a stop to that.

786
00:34:28.817 --> 00:34:30.195
- That's true.

787
00:34:30.196 --> 00:34:31.713
But the cops dropped the ball

788
00:34:31.714 --> 00:34:33.299
isn't a legal defence
for murder.

789
00:34:33.300 --> 00:34:35.126
- I know.
- Public trust

790
00:34:35.127 --> 00:34:36.575
is hanging by a thread.

791
00:34:36.576 --> 00:34:38.057
If we wanna restore it.

792
00:34:38.058 --> 00:34:40.851
you need to bring in
Len's killer. Quickly.

793
00:34:40.852 --> 00:34:43.057
- No one was doing
anything about it.

794
00:34:43.058 --> 00:34:44.678
Maybe this is a vigilante thing.

795
00:34:44.679 --> 00:34:47.954
Maybe somebody found out
what Len did to a loved one

796
00:34:47.955 --> 00:34:49.747
and took matters
into their own hands.

797
00:34:49.748 --> 00:34:52.299
- Now we're looking at friends
and family of six victims.

798
00:34:52.300 --> 00:34:55.126
three of whom we haven't
even identified yet.

799
00:34:55.127 --> 00:34:57.299
- Wonderful. So we're missing
half our suspect pool.

800
00:34:57.300 --> 00:35:00.575
- Yeah. but there's a vigil
in the. uh. village tonight.

801
00:35:00.576 --> 00:35:03.575
If somebody close to one
of our victims killed Len.

802
00:35:03.576 --> 00:35:06.300
well. odds are.
they're gonna be there.

803
00:35:09.783 --> 00:35:11.231
- They were loved.

804
00:35:12.265 --> 00:35:14.264
They are missed

805
00:35:14.265 --> 00:35:15.990
and they should've
been protected.

806
00:35:16.921 --> 00:35:19.264
If you brought something
to leave tonight.

807
00:35:19.265 --> 00:35:21.816
please come forward.
Thank you all for coming.

808
00:35:21.817 --> 00:35:23.748
[somber music]

809
00:35:26.231 --> 00:35:28.333
[sobbing]

810
00:35:28.334 --> 00:35:31.058
[indistinct chatter]

811
00:35:38.714 --> 00:35:40.921
[distant sirens wailing]

812
00:35:46.127 --> 00:35:47.645
- Excuse me.

813
00:35:51.852 --> 00:35:53.817
[intriguing music]

814
00:35:58.093 --> 00:35:59.471
- What is it?

815
00:35:59.472 --> 00:36:01.196
- Omar's dog.

816
00:36:01.748 --> 00:36:03.334
- Ziggy Stardust.

817
00:36:07.300 --> 00:36:09.507
- We're not open
for another hour.

818
00:36:12.472 --> 00:36:13.851
Detectives.

819
00:36:13.852 --> 00:36:15.989
What brings you here?

820
00:36:15.990 --> 00:36:20.713
- We wanted to check in.
Just thinking about you.

821
00:36:20.714 --> 00:36:23.057
It must've been difficult
to learn that the man

822
00:36:23.058 --> 00:36:25.299
you were canvassing with
for months

823
00:36:25.300 --> 00:36:26.851
was responsible for killing

824
00:36:26.852 --> 00:36:28.506
the very men
you were searching for.

825
00:36:28.507 --> 00:36:31.540
- Yeah. I'm still trying
to wrap my head around it.

826
00:36:31.541 --> 00:36:34.023
- Anything strange
stand out about. uh.

827
00:36:34.024 --> 00:36:36.264
Len's behaviour
in hindsight?

828
00:36:36.265 --> 00:36:39.954
- He liked asking people
about Arjun. Yusuf. and Omar.

829
00:36:39.955 --> 00:36:41.438
Too much.

830
00:36:42.507 --> 00:36:44.816
I always felt uneasy about it.

831
00:36:44.817 --> 00:36:46.782
- Good instincts.

832
00:36:46.783 --> 00:36:49.299
Serial killers.
they often insert themselves

833
00:36:49.300 --> 00:36:51.368
in the aftermaths
of their crimes

834
00:36:51.369 --> 00:36:54.057
to relive the thrill
of the kill.

835
00:36:54.058 --> 00:36:57.989
And one other way
they do that is. uh. trophies.

836
00:36:57.990 --> 00:37:00.402
Some like to wear
their victim's jewellery.

837
00:37:00.403 --> 00:37:03.713
Others carry something on them.

838
00:37:03.714 --> 00:37:07.783
ID. keys. a lighter.

839
00:37:11.541 --> 00:37:14.609
- Does this symbol
mean anything to you?

840
00:37:14.610 --> 00:37:16.575
- No.

841
00:37:16.576 --> 00:37:17.851
Never seen that before.

842
00:37:17.852 --> 00:37:19.678
- When I saw it.
I immediately thought

843
00:37:19.679 --> 00:37:21.437
of the lightning bolt

844
00:37:21.438 --> 00:37:24.885
from David Bowie's
Ziggy Stardust era.

845
00:37:24.886 --> 00:37:27.610
The same alter ego that
Omar named his dog after.

846
00:37:28.231 --> 00:37:30.299
So... I got curious.

847
00:37:30.300 --> 00:37:31.816
I wanted to follow up
with his neighbour

848
00:37:31.817 --> 00:37:34.092
to see if she knew
what happened to his dog.

849
00:37:34.093 --> 00:37:37.438
The dog that barked for days
after Omar went missing?

850
00:37:38.817 --> 00:37:41.264
And she said that...

851
00:37:41.265 --> 00:37:43.196
Ziggy went to Omar's sister.

852
00:37:44.369 --> 00:37:45.644
Hazel.

853
00:37:45.645 --> 00:37:47.507
[shaky breathing]

854
00:37:49.024 --> 00:37:51.368
- That's what Omar
used to call me.

855
00:37:51.369 --> 00:37:52.852
His sister.

856
00:37:53.955 --> 00:37:55.333
[sighing]
Neither of us had family

857
00:37:55.334 --> 00:37:58.057
to lean on.
so we looked out for each other.

858
00:37:58.058 --> 00:38:00.333
It wasn't blood. but...

859
00:38:00.334 --> 00:38:02.402
it was real. We chose it.

860
00:38:02.403 --> 00:38:04.438
- Hazel. we spoke to your staff.

861
00:38:05.576 --> 00:38:07.402
The ones who work
at the upstairs bar

862
00:38:07.403 --> 00:38:08.782
and the main bar.

863
00:38:08.783 --> 00:38:11.333
On the night of the drag show.
none of them saw you

864
00:38:11.334 --> 00:38:14.610
after you closed Len's tab.
not until after midnight.

865
00:38:17.507 --> 00:38:19.126
What happened?

866
00:38:19.127 --> 00:38:22.092
[heavy breathing]

867
00:38:22.093 --> 00:38:23.610
[tense music]

868
00:38:26.472 --> 00:38:28.782
- Len brought
the lighter that night

869
00:38:28.783 --> 00:38:31.713
because he knew

870
00:38:31.714 --> 00:38:35.023
he'd be close to someone

871
00:38:35.024 --> 00:38:37.126
who cared about Omar.

872
00:38:37.127 --> 00:38:39.644
You.

873
00:38:39.645 --> 00:38:41.403
He got a thrill out of that.

874
00:38:43.024 --> 00:38:46.023
And as you said. uh.
he overdid it on the drinks.

875
00:38:46.024 --> 00:38:49.645
And when you went to close out
his tab. he finally slipped up.

876
00:38:50.472 --> 00:38:53.369
He pulled that lighter
out with the cash. didn't he?

877
00:38:54.127 --> 00:38:55.713
- You know. I had this
lighter custom printed

878
00:38:55.714 --> 00:38:58.195
for Omar's 40th birthday.

879
00:38:58.196 --> 00:39:00.678
Bowie was his sobriety
inspiration.

880
00:39:00.679 --> 00:39:03.678
[laughing]
He just...

881
00:39:03.679 --> 00:39:05.299
He never. ever lit
a cigarette without it.

882
00:39:05.300 --> 00:39:06.851
He was a...

883
00:39:06.852 --> 00:39:08.886
pack a day guy.

884
00:39:14.507 --> 00:39:17.023
Len rested the lighter
on the counter.

885
00:39:17.024 --> 00:39:19.437
It wasn't even there
for a second.

886
00:39:19.438 --> 00:39:21.162
I recognized it right away.

887
00:39:22.714 --> 00:39:25.783
And then. everything just.
uh... clicked.

888
00:39:27.369 --> 00:39:30.575
Len's enthusiasm when
we would go canvassing.

889
00:39:30.576 --> 00:39:32.195
And the way
he would encourage me

890
00:39:32.196 --> 00:39:34.816
to open up about Omar.

891
00:39:34.817 --> 00:39:38.195
He'd listen. smile.

892
00:39:38.196 --> 00:39:41.024
Looking back on it.
he wasn't comforting me.

893
00:39:41.817 --> 00:39:43.989
He was getting some sort of

894
00:39:43.990 --> 00:39:46.024
sick rise out of my grief.

895
00:39:47.679 --> 00:39:49.817
But I needed to hear him say it.

896
00:39:52.438 --> 00:39:54.162
So I drugged him.

897
00:39:55.231 --> 00:39:57.575
I made Len one last drink.

898
00:39:57.576 --> 00:39:59.541
I swiped some ketamine
from Benji.

899
00:40:00.852 --> 00:40:02.540
I waited 'til he finished it.

900
00:40:02.541 --> 00:40:05.024
Spilled a drink on him.
made it look like an accident.

901
00:40:05.783 --> 00:40:07.540
I watched him walk
to the bathroom.

902
00:40:07.541 --> 00:40:09.644
clean himself off.

903
00:40:09.645 --> 00:40:11.817
That's where I confronted him.

904
00:40:13.576 --> 00:40:15.989
I told him I saw the lighter.

905
00:40:15.990 --> 00:40:17.506
I know you killed them.

906
00:40:17.507 --> 00:40:21.264
His whole demeanour
just shifted.

907
00:40:21.265 --> 00:40:25.092
Just looked me dead
in the eye and he said.

908
00:40:25.093 --> 00:40:26.782
"No one will believe you."

909
00:40:26.783 --> 00:40:30.437
Before I could even process it.
Len slipped away.

910
00:40:30.438 --> 00:40:32.402
But he was right.

911
00:40:32.403 --> 00:40:34.093
I didn't have any proof.

912
00:40:36.024 --> 00:40:39.368
You know. I spent months
sounding the alarm.

913
00:40:39.369 --> 00:40:40.782
Telling anybody who'd listen.

914
00:40:40.783 --> 00:40:43.230
"Someone is targeting men
in the village."

915
00:40:43.231 --> 00:40:46.989
Nobody cared.
Cops didn't care.

916
00:40:46.990 --> 00:40:49.299
Webb didn't care.

917
00:40:49.300 --> 00:40:50.954
Just kept feeding us
the same line

918
00:40:50.955 --> 00:40:52.783
about no signs of foul play.

919
00:40:54.058 --> 00:40:55.714
So I made a decision.

920
00:40:57.196 --> 00:40:59.472
I said.
"I'll give you foul play."

921
00:41:00.576 --> 00:41:02.195
You know. Len mentioned
that he

922
00:41:02.196 --> 00:41:05.093
went through
the Rosedale Trail sometimes.

923
00:41:05.852 --> 00:41:08.195
I knew if he died
in that ravine.

924
00:41:08.196 --> 00:41:10.541
cops wouldn't be able
to ignore it.

925
00:41:11.610 --> 00:41:13.782
They'd have to take it
seriously.

926
00:41:13.783 --> 00:41:15.403
Bring in the real detectives.

927
00:41:17.058 --> 00:41:18.990
So I staged the crime scene.

928
00:41:20.231 --> 00:41:21.817
It's the only way
to get you here.

929
00:41:22.576 --> 00:41:25.747
To make you look at those
missing posters

930
00:41:25.748 --> 00:41:27.782
and see the pattern

931
00:41:27.783 --> 00:41:29.885
and realize that. yes.

932
00:41:29.886 --> 00:41:31.610
Len was a part of this.

933
00:41:35.507 --> 00:41:37.333
I knew once you did.
you'd have to investigate

934
00:41:37.334 --> 00:41:38.921
these cases as connected.

935
00:41:39.955 --> 00:41:42.057
'Til you saw Len
for what he truly was.

936
00:41:42.058 --> 00:41:43.782
- Hazel. you must've known that

937
00:41:43.783 --> 00:41:46.471
once we did learn
the truth about Len.

938
00:41:46.472 --> 00:41:49.437
we would still be looking
for his real killer.

939
00:41:49.438 --> 00:41:51.540
You weren't afraid
that we'd find you?

940
00:41:51.541 --> 00:41:54.506
[weakly]: Yeah.
[sobbing]

941
00:41:54.507 --> 00:41:56.334
I was scared.

942
00:41:59.472 --> 00:42:01.609
But then I thought about Omar.

943
00:42:01.610 --> 00:42:03.541
And how scared he must've been.

944
00:42:04.783 --> 00:42:06.299
And how I couldn't
let that happen

945
00:42:06.300 --> 00:42:08.817
to another vulnerable
person from my community.

946
00:42:11.265 --> 00:42:14.196
Even now.
I'd do it again.

947
00:42:15.990 --> 00:42:18.126
To expose Len.

948
00:42:18.127 --> 00:42:19.990
to find their bodies.

949
00:42:20.990 --> 00:42:23.747
[sighing]

950
00:42:23.748 --> 00:42:26.576
At least
someone's finally listening.

951
00:42:28.990 --> 00:42:31.299
Serial killers
always become famous.

952
00:42:31.300 --> 00:42:33.195
Infamous.

953
00:42:33.196 --> 00:42:35.540
Interviews. podcasts.
books. movies.

954
00:42:35.541 --> 00:42:38.402
all while their victims
become footnotes.

955
00:42:38.403 --> 00:42:40.816
With Len. they're never gonna
be able to tell his story

956
00:42:40.817 --> 00:42:42.921
without talking to me.

957
00:42:44.369 --> 00:42:45.885
And I'm never gonna tell it

958
00:42:45.886 --> 00:42:49.195
without centring every single
one of his victims.

959
00:42:49.196 --> 00:42:52.438
And the cops who didn't even see
them as human enough to care.

960
00:42:54.196 --> 00:42:56.540
[door opening]

961
00:42:56.541 --> 00:42:58.333
[door shutting]

962
00:42:58.334 --> 00:43:00.230
- Hazel Bennett.
you're under arrest

963
00:43:00.231 --> 00:43:01.955
for the murder of Len Marsden.

964
00:43:04.265 --> 00:43:06.264
Read her her rights outside.

965
00:43:06.265 --> 00:43:08.403
[door opening]

966
00:43:11.507 --> 00:43:13.333
[somber music]

967
00:43:13.334 --> 00:43:14.852
[door shutting]

968
00:43:16.369 --> 00:43:18.023
- That doesn't
feel like justice.

969
00:43:18.024 --> 00:43:20.024
- Maybe because it's not.

970
00:43:25.438 --> 00:43:29.299
[theme song]

971
00:43:29.300 --> 00:43:32.610
Subtitling: difuze

971
